    pr_ref:  # 54d6
    description: "F67.A1 (blind severity 3/Moderate). The 3 producer/fallback/runtime coherence linters all walk the package SOURCE tree with ast and check producer call-sites (Edge.create(evidence_type='...')) against the canonical registries. None ever inspects an emitted behavior map, and the run orchestrator never imports them — they are invoked only by a CI wrapper, a property-test helper, and humans. So a long-tail analyzer that emits an incoherent SUBSTRATE (a dangling edge, a bad origin) passes all 3 'coherence' gates as long as its source call-sites use registry-valid literals. The only emit-time gate is the spec_validator, whose validation_report reports zero violations on the substrate and has no dangling-endpoint check. A maintainer trusting that 'coherence' enforcement covers the runtime-emitted graph is wrong: the name oversells a source-call-site gate. Fix: wire emit-time coherence enforcement on the produced graph, or rename to reflect source-only scope. filed via tranch 04 (methodology-comparability run, reused tranch-03 substrate sha a32c4a31)."  # 54d6
